            "title": "Finding the Area of a Triangle",
            "explanation": {
              "text": "The book teaches that the area of a triangle is half the area of a rectangle that has the same base and height: \\(\\text{Area of triangle}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times\\text{Base}\\times\\text{Height}\\). It also states the shortcut \\(\\text{Area of triangle}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times\\text{Area of related rectangle}\\).",
